I drink my water.
The water is cold and nice.
I take my bag from the floor.
I am finished with my break.
I walk up to the counter.
The friendly barista is still standing there.
He looks at me with a smile.
"Would you like anything else?" he asks.
"No thank you," I answer.
"I would like to pay."
"May I ask for the bill?" I ask politely.
"Yes, of course," he says.
He looks at his little screen.
"One black coffee and one cinnamon roll," he says.
"Yes, that is correct," I say.
"Do you want to pay with card or cash?" he asks.
"I would like to pay with a card," I answer.
"Fine."
"That will be eighty-five kroner," he says.
I take out my payment card.
